# Independent continuation correction review (13 October 2026)

The standalone intransitive 続く/transitive 続ける distinction is now explicitly separated from the productive compound ending. The primary curriculum section ～続ける VS ～続く expressly allows both transitive/intransitive and volitional/non-volitional verbs before ～続ける. Thus the corrected rule no longer falsely ties this compound to agentive control. All three examples have valid morphology, readings and meanings: 学ぶ → 学び続ける, 話す → 話し続ける, 降る → 降り続ける. 毎日 supports habitual learning, which the source also permits for the compound; 一時間 supports sustained duration; rain demonstrates a non-volitional process. Oral prompts exactly match stored French translations. The source also accepts 降り続く: the prior rain sentence was not itself ungrammatical. Its replacement now directly illustrates the stated productive 続ける rule. (13 October 2026)

